### TITLE ###
TypingASessionAtThePrompt
### DESCRIPTION ###
The interactive path end to end. One key list drives the whole session, because
the scripted driver carries its events across prompts the way a real terminal
does. FRAMES shows what the user saw, with the caret standing in for the
terminal's own cursor. Ctrl-D on an empty buffer ends it.
### ARGS ###
repl
### KEYS ###
"x = 41"
enter
"x + 1"
enter
ctrl-d
### STDOUT ###
🤙 Rad REPL v0.12.0
Type ':help' for help, ':exit' or Ctrl+D to quit.

