### TITLE ###
BlockEntryIndentsAndTheBlankLineCloses
### DESCRIPTION ###
Enter opens a line instead of running when the buffer is incomplete, and the
indent is supplied for you. The continuation prompt marks the lines that are
still being gathered.
### ARGS ###
repl
### KEYS ###
"if true:"
enter
"print('in')"
enter
enter
ctrl-d
### STDOUT ###
🤙 Rad REPL v0.12.0
Type ':help' for help, ':exit' or Ctrl+D to quit.

