### TITLE ###
CtrlCAbandonsTheLineWithoutEndingTheSession
### DESCRIPTION ###
Ctrl-C throws away what you were typing and gives you a fresh prompt. Nothing
runs, and the session is still there afterwards - which is why the editor
reports a typed outcome rather than a single canceled bit.
### ARGS ###
repl
### KEYS ###
"this would be a syntax error"
ctrl-c
"1 + 1"
enter
ctrl-d
### STDOUT ###
🤙 Rad REPL v0.12.0
Type ':help' for help, ':exit' or Ctrl+D to quit.

